---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts.js';
---
<Layout title="About ConvertKB – Private Image and PDF Tools" description="ConvertKB builds free browser-based tools to compress, resize and convert images and PDFs to the exact size a form asks for, without uploading your files.">
  <div class="narrow pagehead"><h1>About ConvertKB</h1></div>
  <div class="narrow prose" style="padding-bottom:40px">
    <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
    <p>Anyone who has filled in an online application knows the message: "File size must be between 20 KB and 50 KB." The photo is a 4 MB phone picture, the signature is a photo of paper, and the form refuses everything. ConvertKB exists to turn those files into something the form accepts, quickly and without handing your documents to a stranger.</p>
    <h2>How the tools work</h2>
    <p>Every tool runs in your browser. Images are decoded, cropped, resized and re-encoded on your own device; PDFs are read and rebuilt locally; text recognition runs locally after its language pack has downloaded. There is no upload step, so there is no copy of your file on our side.</p>
    <p>For size targets we do not guess. The image tool encodes at different qualities and keeps the highest that fits, shrinking dimensions only when it must. The PDF tool first tries to keep your text and only rebuilds pages as images when that is the only way to reach the limit, and it tells you which happened.</p>
    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <ul><li>We do not store, view or sell your files.</li><li>We do not add watermarks or require an account.</li><li>We do not promise that every portal will accept a file: limits change between application cycles, so each exam page tells you to confirm the numbers against your own notification.</li></ul>
    <h2>Content and accuracy</h2>
    <p>Pages describe typical limits and how files behave at each size. Where figures come from a published notification, we link to the organisation that publishes it. If you spot a number that has changed, please tell us.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions, corrections and feature requests are welcome at <a href={'mailto:' + CONTACT_EMAIL}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
